# FINAL_REPORT.md

Project: *Who guards the guardians when the guardians rotate?* Reproduction of Lee, Iwasa,
Dieckmann and Sigmund (PNAS 2019) and an extension with umpire rotation and inherited integrity.
All numbers below are generated from `results/full/`.

## 1. What was reproduced, and how closely

| Benchmark | Published | Obtained | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| B1 all corrupt | OD 0.25, PC 0.75 | OD {{BoneOD}}, PC {{BonePC}}; max deviation {{BoneDev}} ({{BoneStarts}} random starts) | exact |
| B2 all honest | OC -> 1 | OC -> 1; max deviation {{BtwoDev}} | exact |
| B3 Markov ratio (N = 10) | (19N+87):109 = 2.54 | {{MarkovRatio}}; same closed form from an independent derivation of T | exact |
| B3 simulated ratio | about {{PaperRatio}} | {{BthreeRatio}} [{{BthreeRatioLo}}, {{BthreeRatioHi}}]; rarer exploration: {{BthreeRatioB}}, {{BthreeRatioC}} | close; lower than published; CI excludes 2.15 |
| B4 sustained cycles | about 7 episodes per 1e5 steps (read off) | {{EpisodesSteps}} [{{EpisodesStepsLo}}, {{EpisodesStepsHi}}] | consistent |
| B4 damped oscillations | corrupt about 0.50-0.55 (read off) | {{BfourCorrupt}} [{{BfourCorruptLo}}, {{BfourCorruptHi}}]; stable focus {{FermiRe}} +- {{FermiIm}}i | consistent |
| B4 orbit shrinkage | qualitative | Hopf at mu = nu = {{HopfMuA}} (A = 2), {{HopfMuB}} (A = 0.7) | reproduced |
| Fig. 3C, D values | read off: OC 0.93, PC 0.70, PD 0.45, OD 0.27, period about 137 | at mu = nu = 0.02: {{VioletOC}}, {{VioletPC}}, {{VioletPD}}, {{VioletOD}}, period {{PerViolet}} | match (see D6) |

The fallback project (Section 14 of CLAUDE.md) was not needed: B1 and B2 passed.

## 2. Every discrepancy found
- **D1** Q(y) weighting swapped in the printed Methods (in the PDF itself). Resolved to
  y Q_H + (1 - y) Q_C; the printed form fails B1 (OC -> {{PrintedOC}} with all umpires corrupt).
- **D2** Honest mixed state misnamed "OD+PD (a mixture of OD and PC)"; it is OD and PD.
- **D3** Fig. 3 caption "8 or 9, respectively" reversed relative to the figure; explained by the
  invasion thresholds y_PD = {{yPD}} and y_OD = {{yODA}} (A = 2) or {{yODB}} (A = 0.7).
- **D4** Printed T omits allOD(H) -> allOD(C); transient row, no effect.
- **D5** Printed T gives mu/6 to a neutral player mutant in row 4; transient row, no effect.
- **D6** Fig. 3C, D are labeled as the mu = nu = 1e-4 orbit (period {{PerSlow}}), but match the
  mu = nu = 0.02 orbit.
- **B3 gap** Simulated ratio {{BthreeRatio}} vs published {{PaperRatio}}; most likely due to the
  reconstructed update procedure (SI unavailable).
- **PMC** web version lost minus signs; all signs taken from the PDF.
- **SI** not available (U1-U4 in SPEC.md): IBM update scheme, payoff evaluation, time unit, and
  T derivation were reconstructed or re-derived.

## 3. Hypothesis outcomes (pre-registered rules in METRICS.md)
| Hypothesis | Outcome | Mean field | Finite population |
|---|---|---|---|
| H1 rotation raises honesty, damps cycles | {{OutcomeOne}} | cycles vanish at rho_c = {{RhoC}} (SNIC); honesty {{YbarZero}} -> {{YbarRhoTwenty}} at rho = 0.2 | honesty {{HoneYSZero}} -> {{HoneYSMax}}; episodes {{HoneEpSZero}} -> {{HoneEpSMax}} per 1000 generations |
| H2 vigilance paradox | {{OutcomeTwo}} | PC {{PCZero}} -> {{PCLastCycle}}; peak corruption {{DepthYZero}} -> {{DepthYLast}} | PC {{HtwoPCSZero}} -> {{HtwoPCSThirty}}; lowest cooperation in episodes {{HtwoDCSZero}} -> {{HtwoDCSTen}}; duration {{HtwoRecSZero}} -> {{HtwoRecSThirty}} |
| H3 inheritance weakens rotation | {{OutcomeThree}} | V1 = V0 at rho (1 - kappa), exact; V2, V3 also weaker | honesty falls with kappa for V1, V2, V3; V1 vs V0(rho_eff): {{HthreeNexcl}} of {{HthreeNtests}} CIs exclude 0 ({{HthreeBonf}} after Bonferroni) |
| H4 rotation vs transparency | {{OutcomeFour}} | gain rises with h in {{HfourInc}}/{{HfourPairs}} pairs (honesty); mixed for cooperation | {{HfourIncIBM}}/{{HfourPairsIBM}} pairs |
| H5 conformist bistability | {{OutcomeFive}} | {{HfiveNbi}}/{{HfiveNscan}} bistable in the pre-registered scan; open region only for kappa >= {{HfiveKminDefault}}; no loop in pre-registered sweep, loop post hoc | no dependence on the starting state |
| H6 delay destabilizes | {{OutcomeSix}} | rightmost root <= {{HsixMaxRe}} over {{HsixPoints}} points | not tested separately (mean-field question) |

## 4. Key figures
- `figures/fig04_bifurcation_rho.pdf`: SNIC in rho, period scaling (slope {{SnicSlope}}),
  two-parameter diagram.
- `figures/fig07_vigilance_h2.pdf`: vigilance falls, episodes get shallower (H2).
- `figures/fig06_rho_kappa.pdf`: inheritance weakens rotation (H3).
- `figures/fig01..03`: reproduction. Full list in `figures/README.md`.

## 5. Additional findings
- Small-exploration formula for the critical rotation rate: {{RhoCApprox}} vs exact {{RhoC}};
  rho_c / mu = {{RhoCOverMuA}} (A = 2) and {{RhoCOverMuB}} (A = 0.7).
- rho_c depends non-monotonically on h (peak {{RhoCMax}} near h = {{RhoCMaxH}}, {{RhoCHighH}} at
  h = 0.28) because the PD invasion threshold falls with h.
- Whole-cohort pulses beat continuous rotation at the same mean rate (mean field
  {{PulseMFCont}} -> {{PulseMFFull}}; IBM {{PulseIBMCont}} -> {{PulseIBMFull}}).
- Newcomers who are not reliably honest raise rho_c ({{RhoCpZeroNinety}}, {{RhoCpZeroSeventyFive}},
  {{RhoCpZeroSixty}} for p0 = 0.9, 0.75, 0.6), and with p0 = 0.6 rotation can lower honesty
  (to {{PZeroSixtyMin}}).
- Large populations: honesty with rotation is within {{NeutralMaxDev}} of (nu + rho)/(2 nu + rho).

## 6. Limitations
Reconstructed IBM (SI unavailable); qualitative cross-level comparison (different time units and
imitation rules); well-mixed populations; equal learning rates; simple inheritance rules;
two-player games; global attraction above rho_c shown numerically, not proved; H5 region found by
a follow-up. See REVIEW.md.

## 7. Open items for the author
1. Download the SI Appendix (pnas.1900078116.sapp.pdf) manually, put it in refs/, and check
   SPEC.md items U1-U4; if the update rule differs, rerun `make all`.
2. Fill in the repository URL, email, ORCID and acknowledgements in paper/main.tex and README.
3. Decide whether to keep A = 0.7 and the two-parameter Hopf region in the main text.
4. Consider a formal derivation of rho_c (matched asymptotics) and an analysis of pulses as a
   periodically forced system.
5. Read NOTES_for_author.md before interviews; the answers there are honest about the gaps.

## 8. Exact commands to regenerate everything
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pytest
mingw32-make all            # or: make all (Linux/macOS), or: python run_all.py full
```
Equivalent step by step:
```bash
python experiments/run_reproduction.py full
python experiments/run_extension.py full
python experiments/run_sensitivity.py full
python experiments/evaluate_hypotheses.py full
python experiments/make_figures.py full
python experiments/make_numbers.py full
python experiments/render_docs.py
python experiments/build_paper.py
```
Recorded compute: about {{RuntimeFullMin}} minutes (full) and {{RuntimeQuickMin}} minutes (quick).

